<title>USA: SurVivaLink names Wagner chief executive.</title>
<headline>SurVivaLink names Wagner chief executive.</headline>
<dateline>MINNEAPOLIS 1997-01-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>SurVivaLink Corp said Monday it has named its president and chief operating officer Mark Wagner as chief executive officer.</p>
<p>Wagner replaces Byron Gilman, who will remain chairman and assume the title and duties of chief technical officer. </p>
<p>Wagner joined SurVivaLink in September 1996.</p>
<p>SurVivaLink provides automated external defribillators used to treat victims of sudden cardiac arrest.</p>
<p>((--Chicago newsdesk, 312-408-8787))</p>
